From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pi-bolt <pi-bolt@localhost>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:31:58 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Pi-Bolt: module-state snapshot prototype: audit, record and
 replay of bundled modules' top-level state

BUN_MODULE_SNAPSHOT_WRAP=1 at build time wraps every bundled ES module (__esm) and hooks the runtime's __esm and __commonJS
helpers into bun:pibolt-snapshot (PiBoltSnapshot.cpp). BUN_MODULE_SNAPSHOT_AUDIT=file records, per module, its own
instructions, the cells it made, the chunk variables it set, what it read of the environment and whatever it changed that
it did not make. BUN_MODULE_SNAPSHOT_OUT=file with BUN_MODULE_SNAPSHOT_MODULES=list writes the listed modules' state as
operations; <executable>.msnap is replayed when such a module would run (BUN_MODULE_SNAPSHOT=0: never;
BUN_MODULE_SNAPSHOT_CHECK=1: each replay written again and compared). Research prototype: replay is not cheaper than the
modules' ahead-of-time compiled code, and wrapping costs more than it saves. Nothing changes without the variables.
